<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Narendranagar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Narendranagar is a town in the Tehri <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/garhwal">Garhwal</a> district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uttarakhand">Uttarakhand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the hills above Rishikesh. It was founded in the early 20th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharaja</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narendra-shah">Narendra Shah</a> of Tehri Garhwal State, who moved his capital there from Tehri and named it after himself. His palace was later converted into a spa resort.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/narendranagar.jpg" alt="Narendranagar" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.flickr.com/photos/peem/ · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Himalayan_view_from_Ananda_spa,_Narendra_Nagar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
